WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.293
Lab 2 runs the rule in your own
test tenant: worldwide or G C C,

2
00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:08.270
with a test Active Directory
domain, never production,

3
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.513
with fictional people, and with
Module 1's Lab 2 already run.

4
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:16.429
Make two test orphans: an app
registration with no owners,

5
00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:18.262
and a test service account.

6
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:21.987
Run the check with an app that
holds only User dot Read dot All.

7
00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.663
Confirm both orphans as the
identity governance officer.

8
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:28.396
Then have a second person
approve the plan's hash,

9
00:00:28.396 --> 00:00:31.538
which is the separation of
duties the evidence records.

10
00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:33.379
Dry-run the plan, then apply it,

11
00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:37.213
signed in as a person with
Cloud Application Administrator.

12
00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:40.936
To back it out, step six turns
the service principal back on,

13
00:00:40.936 --> 00:00:44.271
enables the test account,
deletes both test objects

14
00:00:44.271 --> 00:00:47.762
and the test app's registration,
and deletes the output.

15
00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:49.970
The authors haven't run Lab 2.
